research/audit/wave0-abstract-algebra.provenance.jsonl-34-{"id":"ex-symmetric-group-on-three-letters","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Symmetric_group","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dihedral_group_of_order_6"],"rationale":"Sourced: S3 has six elements, is the first nonabelian symmetric group, and its elements are the identity (order 1), three transpositions (order 2) and two 3-cycles (order 3). Delta: the item works with the specific set {1,2,3} of von Neumann naturals and proves exhaustiveness of the six listed triples by hand. Verification written locally.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-02"}
research/audit/wave0-abstract-algebra.provenance.jsonl-35-{"id":"cex-power-of-a-product-in-a-nonabelian-group","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exponentiation","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Symmetric_group"],"rationale":"Sourced: the exponent law (bc)^n = b^n c^n is \"true only if the summands commute\", and S3 is non-abelian with the transpositions as witnesses. The witness pair g = (1 2), h = (2 3) with n = 2 is a directly checkable instance of that caveat rather than a new claim. Refutation written locally.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-02"}
research/audit/wave0-abstract-algebra.provenance.jsonl-36-{"id":"ex-klein-four-group","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Klein_four-group","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Symmetric_group"],"rationale":"The source states exactly this realisation: \"The identity and double-transpositions of four objects form V\", i.e. {(), (1,2)(3,4), (1,3)(2,4), (1,4)(2,3)} inside S4; four elements; abelian, with \"composing any two of the three non-identity elements produces the third one\" (the item multiplication table); \"All non-identity elements of the Klein group have order 2\"; and \"The Klein four-group is the smallest non-cyclic group\". Same hypotheses, same conventions, cosmetic differences only. Verification written locally.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-02"}
research/audit/wave0-abstract-algebra.provenance.jsonl:37:{"id":"ex-symmetries-of-a-square","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dihedral_group","https://www.whitman.edu/documents/Academics/Mathematics/2014/rodriglr.pdf"],"rationale":"Sourced: the dihedral group of order 8, presentation r^4 = s^2 = 1 with srs = r^-1 (equivalently sr = r^-1 s), elements {e, r, r^2, r^3, s, rs, r^2 s, r^3 s}, non-abelian, the symmetry group of the square; and the standard graph-theoretic fact Aut(C_n) = D_n, which is claim 4 at n = 4. Convention delta recorded: the square is COMBINATORIAL here (a 4-cycle edge relation on {1,2,3,4}), not Euclidean, because R^2 is not available at this point in the reading order, so claim 4 is Aut(C_4) = D_4 rendered as a permutation identity. Verification written locally.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-02"}
research/audit/wave0-abstract-algebra.provenance.jsonl-38-{"id":"ex-subgroups-of-the-integers","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyclic_group","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Subgroup"],"rationale":"Sourced: \"all subgroups of Z are of the form <m> = mZ\" and every subgroup of a cyclic group is cyclic. Delta: the item states the converse half with n >= 0, identifies n as the least positive element of H when H is nontrivial, and handles H = {0} separately. Verification written locally, driven by the least-positive-element argument and division with remainder.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-02"}
research/audit/wave0-abstract-algebra.provenance.jsonl-39-{"id":"cex-subset-closed-under-the-operation-not-a-subgroup","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Subgroup","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monoid#Submonoids","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cancellation_property"],"rationale":"Sourced: the nonnegative integers under addition are a submonoid of (Z,+) that is not a group (\"the non-negative integers form a cancellative monoid under addition ... yet lack additive inverses required for group structure\"), which is exactly the witness used. The refuted claim (nonempty + contains the identity + closed under the operation implies subgroup) is the standard motivation for testing xy^-1 rather than xy. Refutation written locally. Note: the Cancellation_property URL is the sharpest support and is NOT currently in this item sources.references; the two URLs that are there also return 200.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-02"}
research/audit/wave0-abstract-algebra.provenance.jsonl-40-{"id":"fs-union-of-two-subgroups-is-a-subgroup","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Subgroup","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Union_(set_theory)"],"rationale":"The source states the false claim, the exact criterion and the exact witness: \"The union of subgroups A and B is a subgroup if and only if A subset B or B subset A\", with the counterexample that 2Z union 3Z is not a subgroup of Z because 2 and 3 lie in it but 5 does not. The item reproduces that statement, that witness and that criterion with no change of hypotheses or conventions. Refutation written locally.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-02"}
