research/audit/wave4-foundations.provenance.jsonl:30:{"id": "ex-the-cofinality-of-aleph-omega", "statement": "ai-altered", "proof": "ai-altered", "evidence": "semantic-source", "urls": ["https://www.homepages.ucl.ac.uk/~ucahcjm/ast/ast_notes_4.pdf"], "rationale": "The source gives the general limit-index identity cf(aleph_alpha)=cf(alpha). The item specializes it to alpha=omega, names the exact cofinal set C={aleph_n:n in omega}, and expands the choice-free upper- and lower-bound verification. At A4 the model-side fetch resolved the UCL PDF with HTTP 200 and exposed the cited mathematical text. A6 URL disposition (Alpha, 2026-08-04): the recorded www.ucl.ac.uk path returns HTTP 404; the same notes are live at www.homepages.ucl.ac.uk, fetched at HTTP 200 and confirmed to be Chapter 4, Cardinal Arithmetic, whose section 4.4 defines cofinality, regular and singular cardinals and computes cf(aleph_omega) = omega. The URL was rewritten in the item and here; the source itself is unchanged.", "alpha_concurred": false, "at": "2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-foundations.provenance.jsonl:31:{"id": "ex-a-singular-cardinal-of-uncountable-cofinality", "statement": "ai-altered", "proof": "ai-altered", "evidence": "semantic-source", "urls": ["https://www.homepages.ucl.ac.uk/~ucahcjm/ast/ast_notes_4.pdf"], "rationale": "The source gives the general limit-index identity cf(aleph_alpha)=cf(alpha), whose alpha=omega_1 instance is the displayed result. The item weakens the ambient hypothesis to AC_omega and writes out the bounded-countable-subset argument, so the hypothesis convention is not exact. At A4 the model-side fetch resolved the UCL PDF with HTTP 200 and exposed the cited mathematical text. A6 URL disposition (Alpha, 2026-08-04): the recorded www.ucl.ac.uk path returns HTTP 404; the same notes are live at www.homepages.ucl.ac.uk, fetched at HTTP 200 and confirmed to be Chapter 4, Cardinal Arithmetic, whose section 4.4 defines cofinality, regular and singular cardinals and computes cf(aleph_omega) = omega. The URL was rewritten in the item and here; the source itself is unchanged.", "alpha_concurred": false, "at": "2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-foundations.provenance.jsonl-32-{"id": "ex-an-aleph-fixed-point", "statement": "ai-altered", "proof": "ai-altered", "evidence": "semantic-source", "urls": ["https://math.osu.edu/~derdzinski.1/courses/5001/fixed-points.pdf"], "rationale": "The sources construct aleph fixed points by omega iteration of the continuous aleph operation, including singular fixed points of countable cofinality. The item selects the tower starting at aleph_0 and expands both the fixed-point and cofinality checks. At A4 the model-side fetch resolved the Ohio State PDF with HTTP 200 and exposed the cited fixed-point construction.", "alpha_concurred": false, "at": "2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-foundations.provenance.jsonl-33-{"id": "ex-the-beth-hierarchy-computed", "statement": "ai-generated", "proof": "ai-generated", "evidence": "trivial", "urls": [], "rationale": "The exact bundle is a bespoke unwinding of the beth definition: the first three values follow by substitution and power-set cardinality, and the beth_omega cofinality computation repeats the cited limit-sequence argument.", "alpha_concurred": false, "at": "2026-08-04"}
